0..79 Comment "//! An extension type stated as the signature the face theory generates for it."
80..159 Comment "//! `ext Val on left is zero` over the two points of `Two` is the type of cells"
160..236 Comment "//! fixed to `zero` on the face `left`: a cell holds its value off the face,"
237..316 Comment "//! `ins` introduces it and `outp`, `outq` read it at each point. The boundary,"
317..398 Comment "//! β and η are the signature\'s laws, so each holds by conversion, on a neutral"
399..431 Comment "//! cell as on an introduced one"
432..512 Comment "//! [Zhang-2024-three_noncubical_applications_extension_types]. The member `ext`"
513..580 Comment "//! generates this signature from its spelling (`generated.gandr`)."
581..584 Comment "//!"
585..656 Comment "//! - cites: [Zhang-2024-three_noncubical_applications_extension_types]"
657..660 Comment "//!"
661..816 Comment "//! [Zhang-2024-three_noncubical_applications_extension_types]: https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.05658 \"Zhang, Three non-cubical applications of extension types\""
818..894 Comment "/// The cells of `Val` over `Two` fixed to `zero` on `left`, with `c` a cell"
895..973 Comment "/// nothing introduces. The boundary reads `zero` at `left` of every cell, `c`"
974..1053 Comment "/// included; β reads an introduced cell\'s value at the point off the face; η"
1054..1095 Comment "/// rebuilds a cell from its value there."
1096..1098 Other "@["
1099..1109 Other "normalizes"
1109..1110 Other "("
1110..1111 StringLit "\""
1111..1178 StringLit "cells(outp(c), outq(ins(one)), ins(outq(c))) ~> cells(zero, one, c)"
1178..1179 StringLit "\""
1179..1180 Other ")"
1181..1182 Other "]"
